From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:12:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Paint corner-shape on backgrounds and clips

Stylo computes corner-*-shape, but every box path was built from
elliptical arcs, so a bevel, scoop, notch or squircle corner painted
round. When a visible corner is shaped, the border-box, padding-box and
content-box paths now come from a superellipse contour ported from WPT's
render-corner-shape.js reference, which follows Blink: the inner edges
move along the same approximate normal the reference uses, so test and
reference agree. Boxes with only round corners keep their arc paths
unchanged.

Upstream paints backgrounds, overflow clips and masks with
NonUniformRoundedRect shapes, which cannot express a shaped corner. The
new BoxShape carries either that rect or the contour, and the
*_box_clip() accessors pick the contour when a corner is shaped. Box
shadows still use the rounded rect, so a shaped box casts a round
shadow.
